</style><style>@import url('https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/katex@0.16.25/dist/katex-swap.min.css')</style></head><body><article id="3f2193b0-ab57-8087-8745-fee6b32689be" class="page sans"><header><h1 class="page-title" dir="auto"></h1><p class="page-description" dir="auto"></p></header><div class="page-body"><figure id="3f2193b0-ab57-80e8-9335-e2756d153ba9" class="image" data-notion-image="Untitled/title_-_medium.png" dir="ltr"><a href="Untitled/title_-_medium.png"><img style="width:704px" src="Untitled/title_-_medium.png"/></a></figure><h1 id="3f2193b0-ab57-80b0-b1d2-ebeeb339d0de" class="" dir="auto">Feature Wiki &amp; Mechanics Guide</h1><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-8057-b7ff-eb155fca8b2d" class="" dir="auto">Welcome to the Better Combat datapack wiki! This guide explains all features, reworked mechanics, and weapon differences in a clear, user-friendly way.</p><hr id="3f2193b0-ab57-80d0-8b12-ebcf42d4f22e" dir="auto"/><h2 id="3f2193b0-ab57-80d3-82a5-d8db2aca22d2" class="" dir="auto">The Attacking State</h2><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-80af-abcc-f72881ec029b" class="" dir="auto">The combat system activates automatically whenever you hold an eligible weapon (Swords, Axes, Scythes).<br/>While in the <strong>Attacking State</strong>, you will notice key improvements over vanilla combat:</p><ul id="3f2193b0-ab57-8023-a304-c1beb884d59f" class="bulleted-list" dir="auto"><li style="list-style-type:disc"><strong>Attack Indicator:</strong> A red indicator is going to appear over the entities that shows exactly where your strike will land.</li></ul><ul id="3f2193b0-ab57-802a-b41f-ed00f25f4bcd" class="bulleted-list" dir="auto"><li style="list-style-type:disc"><strong>Area Attacks:</strong> Instead of relying only on the standard vanilla system, weapons will let you project a frontal attack area where your hits will land.</li></ul><hr id="3f2193b0-ab57-8067-9984-d32f175f8eaa" dir="auto"/><h2 id="3f2193b0-ab57-804c-8f52-e197fee3b40e" class="" dir="auto">Untouchables</h2><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-8010-a2dd-c8aab131c1ef" class="" dir="auto">To prevent unwanted friendly damage (such as accidentally striking your pet or a villager while fighting off monsters), the datapack has an <strong>untouchables</strong> entity list that won&#x27;t take damage from your area attaccks (although if you don&#x27;t use a reworked weapon you will still hit them).<br/>If you intentionally want to hit an untouchable mob, simply sneak while attacking.</p><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-8041-a1ef-fd9240b44482" class="" dir="auto">List:</p><ul id="3f2193b0-ab57-80fc-ac54-d48876107f46" class="bulleted-list" dir="auto"><li style="list-style-type:disc">Villagers</li></ul><ul id="3f2193b0-ab57-8005-8a92-ca09556ebd5b" class="bulleted-list" dir="auto"><li style="list-style-type:disc">Golems</li></ul><ul id="3f2193b0-ab57-8056-97d3-d064bd5cf756" class="bulleted-list" dir="auto"><li style="list-style-type:disc">Tamed mobs</li></ul><ul id="3f2193b0-ab57-80ca-93f5-ee26762a236f" class="bulleted-list" dir="auto"><li style="list-style-type:disc">Baby mobs</li></ul><ul id="3f2193b0-ab57-80ed-8630-f7c3582aba51" class="bulleted-list" dir="auto"><li style="list-style-type:disc">Zombified Piglins</li></ul><ul id="3f2193b0-ab57-80d6-bd70-d80233a3c962" class="bulleted-list" dir="auto"><li style="list-style-type:disc">Name-tagged entities</li></ul><hr id="3f2193b0-ab57-80c7-ad46-c27bf72df4f2" dir="auto"/><h2 id="3f2193b0-ab57-80cd-b17b-d29d2c60655a" class="" dir="auto">Swords</h2><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-80b3-9516-fe3177af0f5e" class="" dir="auto">Swords are the premier crowd-control weapon, built to handle groups of enemies efficiently. The weak vanilla sweeping effect has been replaced with full-damage area coverage.</p><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-80ba-be92-d9c1652f8ec9" class="" dir="auto"><strong>Range</strong>: 3.0 blocks</p><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-809f-a523-d7ab384119b6" class="" dir="auto"><strong>Normal Attack:</strong><br/>A wide frontal swing. Unlike vanilla sweeping (which deals minimal area damage), this attack hits <em>all</em> valid enemies in the sweep area for <strong>100% of your weapon&#x27;s base damage</strong>.</p><blockquote id="3f2193b0-ab57-80be-b9c0-c35acfb7d081" class="" dir="auto"><figure id="3f3193b0-ab57-8030-99a5-debc92d0bdb1" class="image" data-notion-image="Untitled/sword-normal.gif" dir="ltr"><a href="Untitled/sword-normal.gif"><img style="width:384px" src="Untitled/sword-normal.gif"/></a></figure></blockquote><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-80ed-97a2-eab4f0f86b03" class="" dir="auto"><strong>Sprint Attack:</strong><br/>Instead of hitting an entire area, it targets <strong>only the nearest enemy</strong>, applying standard <strong>bonus sprint knockback</strong> to push dangerous threats away.</p><blockquote id="3f2193b0-ab57-8004-bd20-d445eb3760ac" class="" dir="auto"><figure id="3f3193b0-ab57-8018-8c8f-eea53612f356" class="image" data-notion-image="Untitled/sword-sprint.gif" dir="ltr"><a href="Untitled/sword-sprint.gif"><img style="width:384px" src="Untitled/sword-sprint.gif"/></a></figure></blockquote><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-8088-91db-f453a24633c0" class="" dir="auto"><strong>Critical Attack:</strong><br/>A heavy downward strike executed while falling. Like the sprint attack, this focuses on <strong>only the nearest enemy</strong>, applying bonus damage (+50%).</p><blockquote id="3f2193b0-ab57-80e3-b1f6-c97eab23d4e5" class="" dir="auto"><figure id="3f3193b0-ab57-8006-bcc5-d56a50e28049" class="image" data-notion-image="Untitled/sword-normal%201.gif" dir="ltr"><a href="Untitled/sword-normal%201.gif"><img style="width:384px" src="Untitled/sword-normal%201.gif"/></a></figure></blockquote><hr id="3f2193b0-ab57-8035-9cfb-dd1913fabb1a" dir="auto"/><h2 id="3f2193b0-ab57-801d-84a6-d4d79fae68eb" class="" dir="auto">Axes</h2><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-80fe-b351-c88e1e59526c" class="" dir="auto">Axes represent hard-hitting, high-precision weapons tailored for single-target combat.<br/>Axes can now receive traditional sword combat enchantments (such as <em>Sharpness</em>) via the enchanting table!<br/>If an axe is enchanted with a fighting enchant, its texture becomes a Battle Axe.</p><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-80a9-a9a8-d77edf00de8f" class="" dir="auto"><strong>Range</strong>: 3.0 blocks</p><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-80c2-a670-fca967ebc941" class="" dir="auto"><strong>Normal Attack:</strong><br/>Unlike swords, normal axe attacks do <strong>not</strong> sweep across multiple targets. An axe strike hits <strong>only the single nearest enemy</strong>.</p><blockquote id="3f2193b0-ab57-8088-9e4d-c816e5b5d952" class="" dir="auto"><figure id="3f3193b0-ab57-80fb-be60-f03f7dfdadc6" class="image" data-notion-image="Untitled/axe-normal.gif" dir="ltr"><a href="Untitled/axe-normal.gif"><img style="width:384px" src="Untitled/axe-normal.gif"/></a></figure></blockquote><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-8042-b22a-ce687085c9ae" class="" dir="auto"><strong>Sprint Attack:</strong><br/>A single-target strike that delivers <strong>bonus sprint knockback</strong>.</p><blockquote id="3f2193b0-ab57-8071-9fae-c818d999265b" class="" dir="auto"><figure id="3f3193b0-ab57-809a-8c69-eb8121af3d9c" class="image" data-notion-image="Untitled/axe-sprint.gif" dir="ltr"><a href="Untitled/axe-sprint.gif"><img style="width:384px" src="Untitled/axe-sprint.gif"/></a></figure></blockquote><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-8022-8608-d1f8b9029b05" class="" dir="auto"><strong>Critical Attack:</strong><br/>A heavy downward strike executed while falling. Like the sprint attack, this focuses on <strong>only the nearest enemy</strong>, applying bonus damage (+50%).</p><blockquote id="3f2193b0-ab57-80b6-8d24-e01c6d81c990" class="" dir="auto"><figure id="3f3193b0-ab57-8021-8a2f-fb275574ff34" class="image" data-notion-image="Untitled/axe-crit.gif" dir="ltr"><a href="Untitled/axe-crit.gif"><img style="width:384px" src="Untitled/axe-crit.gif"/></a></figure></blockquote><hr id="3f2193b0-ab57-80f6-891e-c20c3a66366d" dir="auto"/><h2 id="3f2193b0-ab57-8017-96f3-f7276ab6ab0b" class="" dir="auto">Hoes &amp; Scythes</h2><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-8087-8eb9-cdcf576af829" class="" dir="auto">Hoes are now viable combat alternatives, serving as technical, extended-range weapons.<br/>Hoes can now receive traditional sword combat enchantments (such as <em>Sharpness</em>) via the enchanting table!<br/>If an hoe is enchanted with a fighting enchant, its texture becomes a Scythe.</p><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-80e2-8644-fbc498064ebe" class="" dir="auto"><strong>Range</strong>: 4.0 blocks</p><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-8058-9bc9-c3c18f6a8209" class="" dir="auto"><strong>Attack speed</strong>: 3</p><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-8077-bdc5-c61bdeff0929" class="" dir="auto"><mark class="highlight-default" data-notion-highlight="default"><strong>Damage by tiers</strong></mark><mark class="highlight-default" data-notion-highlight="default">:</mark><div class="indented"><details id="3f2193b0-ab57-802e-acc0-ea195f72b038" open="" class="toggle" dir="auto"><summary>show</summary><div class="indented"><div id="3f2193b0-ab57-804b-8db8-e70d7bb65b5f" class="column-list" data-notion-column-list="" dir="auto"><div id="3f2193b0-ab57-802c-818c-f1ab43c0d801" style="width:100%" class="column" data-notion-column-ratio="1" dir="auto"><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-8052-97d3-f339c1a880f0" class="" dir="auto">Wooden: </p><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-8059-bae0-df238d121a76" class="" dir="auto">Stone: </p><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-807e-a25d-cea41c5a0478" class="" dir="auto">Copper: </p><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-809d-bac6-ec9226aca8d0" class="" dir="auto">Golden: </p><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-805b-9603-ca545220f126" class="" dir="auto">Iron: </p><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-802f-a9cf-c2be5f3b1b60" class="" dir="auto">Diamond: </p><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-8031-9206-f106686e2162" class="" dir="auto">Netherite: </p></div><div id="3f2193b0-ab57-80c1-889f-e874829ac12a" style="width:100%" class="column" data-notion-column-ratio="1" dir="auto"><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-8079-ac31-df4e0b0d0c6e" class="" dir="auto">2</p><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-809b-8360-eff38dd9589b" class="" dir="auto">2</p><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-807a-902a-e575e35fc6b4" class="" dir="auto">3</p><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-8026-add9-e62b83303311" class="" dir="auto">2</p><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-80e6-b48b-feea228fe114" class="" dir="auto">3</p><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-80c7-95d7-c953dc17e2c1" class="" dir="auto">4</p><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-801a-87c5-c5b86fa7b38c" class="" dir="auto">4</p></div></div></div></details></div></p><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-8076-a91e-d7cd08f6eb27" class="" dir="auto"><strong>Normal Attack:</strong><br/>A massive sweep attack with superior range. Its signature feature is the <strong>low knockback</strong>. Instead of scattering enemies across the area, it deals damage while keeping foes grouped in place, allowing you to chain consecutive combo hits with ease.</p><blockquote id="3f2193b0-ab57-80d1-b29a-ef89dee6bde9" class="" dir="auto"><figure id="3f3193b0-ab57-800a-9b93-efeb4610d003" class="image" data-notion-image="Untitled/scythe-normal.gif" dir="ltr"><a href="Untitled/scythe-normal.gif"><img style="width:384px" src="Untitled/scythe-normal.gif"/></a></figure></blockquote><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-801c-9773-f4a1bbe70ca0" class="" dir="auto"><strong>Sprint Attack:</strong><br/>Still sprinting lets you apply <strong>bonus sprint knockback</strong> to only the nearest target.</p><blockquote id="3f2193b0-ab57-8014-a18d-e610e2de5764" class="" dir="auto"><figure id="3f3193b0-ab57-8067-a0ee-dc45d99fb862" class="image" data-notion-image="Untitled/scythe-sprint.gif" dir="ltr"><a href="Untitled/scythe-sprint.gif"><img style="width:384px" src="Untitled/scythe-sprint.gif"/></a></figure></blockquote><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-8032-a9fc-dd1965905974" class="" dir="auto"><strong>Critical Attack:</strong><br/>A focused single-target strike. It benefits from the falling critical damage bonus (+50%) while preserving the <strong>low knockback</strong> profile of normal attacks.</p><blockquote id="3f2193b0-ab57-80f1-8a57-f5ff3274ffd4" class="" dir="auto"><figure id="3f3193b0-ab57-80dc-9e21-ed77efe7b66b" class="image" data-notion-image="Untitled/scythe-crit.gif" dir="ltr"><a href="Untitled/scythe-crit.gif"><img style="width:384px" src="Untitled/scythe-crit.gif"/></a></figure></blockquote><hr id="3f2193b0-ab57-8063-bd10-c6d355b78cc1" dir="auto"/><h2 id="3f2193b0-ab57-8058-a4d1-e454f83213fd" class="" dir="auto">Spears</h2><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-801c-bca0-e1e099a50fb1" class="" dir="auto">Spears remain almost untouched from vanilla: the attack speed has been tweeked to be the same throughout different tiers.</p><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-80d2-9be3-d1b7f0ff1959" class="" dir="auto">Attack speed: 1.5</p><blockquote id="3f3193b0-ab57-800a-a9a7-feacee9cde29" class="" dir="auto"><figure id="3f3193b0-ab57-808d-a06b-e04b6bd07665" class="image" data-notion-image="Untitled/spear-normal.gif" dir="ltr"><a href="Untitled/spear-normal.gif"><img style="width:384px" src="Untitled/spear-normal.gif"/></a></figure></blockquote><p id="3f2193b0-ab57-8086-aada-d14e8598e939" class="" dir="auto">
</p><hr id="3f2193b0-ab57-80bd-a299-e9648988687c" dir="auto"/><h2 id="3f2193b0-ab57-80ba-bfca-f64ea6a6f2b8" class="" dir="auto">Enchantments</h2><ul id="3f2193b0-ab57-80ab-af02-ffcdd3c7dda3" class="bulleted-list" dir="auto"><li style="list-style-type:disc"><strong>Sweeping Edge</strong>: this enchantment is no more since all sweeping attacks now deal by default 100% of the weapon&#x27;s damage.</li></ul><ul id="3f2193b0-ab57-8055-9f5e-f05a2dbdcda6" class="bulleted-list" dir="auto"><li style="list-style-type:disc"><strong>Knockback</strong>: the knockback enchant won&#x27;t add bonus knockback while doing Normal Attacks, but will add additional bonus knockback on Sprint Attacks.</li></ul><ul id="3f2193b0-ab57-80b8-8ce5-ce397319f21d" class="bulleted-list" dir="auto"><li style="list-style-type:disc"><strong>Impaling</strong>: Now the impaling enchant will <strong>add damage to all entities touching water</strong> (Bedrock edition parity), instead of damaging only water-based entities.</li></ul><ul id="3f2193b0-ab57-80e5-957b-e7a1546c6e5f" class="bulleted-list" dir="auto"><li style="list-style-type:disc"><strong>Smite &amp; Bane of Arthropods</strong>: These work just like vanilla, but due to Minecraft&#x27;s limitations if just one non-effected entity is present in the attacking area, the damage bonus won&#x27;t be applied to any of the entities. This isn&#x27;t an intented feature and is marked as a bug.</li></ul><ul id="3f2193b0-ab57-809b-b53a-e7623c8b4fe4" class="bulleted-list" dir="auto"><li style="list-style-type:disc"><strong>Axes and hoes</strong>: These tools can also be enchanted with combat enchantments; when it heppeans its textures become respectively a Battle Axe or a Scythe.</li></ul><blockquote id="3f2193b0-ab57-8096-a7ef-c656a7e10eed" class="" dir="auto"><figure id="3f3193b0-ab57-80d1-924b-f5ca746b8fdf" class="image" data-notion-image="Untitled/enchanting.gif" dir="ltr"><a href="Untitled/enchanting.gif"><img style="width:657px" src="Untitled/enchanting.gif"/></a></figure></blockquote></div></article><span class="sans" style="font-size:14px;padding-top:2em"></span></body></html>
